description:
[narrowed from hopeless-branch-skips-scoring-insert-push] Gaps in a hopeless category are dropped before scoring, so 23 documentation_drift gaps that already compute to landability 1.00 — the joint top of ~295 open gaps — are never selected. In pickMostLandable the loop escalates a hopeless gap to a human via uiQuestion_write and then executes `continue`, so it never reaches actionableGaps. PREFERRED CHANGE, AND IT IS AN ADDITION: insert the single line `      actionableGaps.push(g);` immediately BEFORE the existing `      continue;` inside that branch. The hopeless gap is then pushed and the following continue merely skips the loop tail, whose only remaining statement is that same push — verified against the live file, the for-body contains nothing after the if-block except `actionableGaps.push(g);`. Net behaviour is identical to deleting the continue: hopeless gaps reach scoring, the escalation still fires, the existing failed_attempts penalty ranks them beneath healthier work. That is exactly the 're-test path (penalty, not hard exclusion)' the comment above hopeless() already promises and the code does not deliver. WHY THE ADDITION FRAMING: six attempts to DELETE this line failed on 2026-08-26 while three ADDITIONS to the same file landed cleanly. The failures were a patch to the wrong function citing an invented symbol; a comment placed beside the line, hard-failed as 'zero behaviour delta'; a create_file op with an 11-byte body against a 181KB existing file; a whitespace-only edit 1400 lines away; and two anchor misses. Do not delete anything, do not comment anything out, do not use create_file. Insert one line with six leading spaces. ACCEPTED CONSEQUENCE: 11 categories become selectable again, including 23 documentation_drift gaps roughly 82 percent of whose individual claims are false owing to a separate enumeration defect. Bounded and non-destructive — doc_drift_fix is triage-only while DOC_FIX_AUTOLAND is unset, so those gaps yield proposals for a human and never write to any document.

WHY PREVIOUS ATTEMPTS ON THIS GAP FAILED (most recent last):
- anchor_not_found: {"error":"no_unique_anchor: refused fs_edit — planned anchor is non-unique and re-derivation found no unique substring (would mislocalize to first occurrence)"}
- compose_execution_failure: {"error":"no_unique_anchor: refused fs_edit — planned anchor is non-unique and re-derivation found no unique substring (would mislocalize to first occurrence)"}
- compose_execution_failure: {"error":"no_unique_anchor: refused fs_edit — planned anchor is non-unique and re-derivation found no unique substring (would mislocalize to first occurrence)"}

Do not repeat these failures. Address the specific cause named above. [RETRY CONTEXT — compose for gap hopeless-branch-skips-scoring-insert-push-narrowed repeated already-recorded failure class compose_execution_failure: {"error":"no_unique_anchor: refused fs_edit — planned anchor is non-unique and re-derivation found no unique substring (would mislocalize to first occ. The specification is above; this failure text is context only and is not the specification.]

